<title>ITALY: Italy offers 13.0 trln lire of BOTs for sale.</title>
<headline>Italy offers 13.0 trln lire of BOTs for sale.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian treasury said it was offering 13.0 trillion lire of short term bills (BOT), replacing 14.5 trillion lire of expiring paper.</p>
<p>A Treasury statement said it would offer:</p>
<p>* 3.5 trillion lire of three-month BOTs</p>
<p>* 4.5 trillion lire of six-month paper</p>
<p>* 5.0 trillion lire of one-year bills.</p>
<p>Subscriptions close at 1100 GMT on August 11.</p>
<p>The treasury added that it would offer 1.5 trillion lire of two-year zero couponed certificates (CTZ) and 1.5 trillion lire of 18-month CTZ.</p>
<p>Subscriptions for both those sales also close at 1100 GMT, August 11.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782505</p>
</text>
